cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "WAMCES in Python"
message: >-
  This repository is a port. If you use it, please cite the article of the original
  model under preferred-citation. Please cite the Zenodo record of the model as well.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kohlhaas
    given-names: Stephan
    email: stephan.kohlhaas@tum.de
    affiliation: "Technical University of Munich"
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/stkotum/wamces-python"
abstract: >-
  A Python port of WAMCES, the dynamic model of the continental European power
  system by R. Musca: 3809 buses, 618 synchronous machines with voltage regulators,
  stabilisers and governors, 300 grid-forming and 500 grid-following converters
  and 1573 PMUs with a central unit. It needs only numpy and reproduces every state
  of the published Simulink model at every step to 8e-12 of its largest value.
keywords:
  - power systems
  - frequency dynamics
  - wide-area monitoring and control
  - grid-forming converters
  - continental Europe

preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "Dynamic Model of the European Power System for Wide-Area Monitoring and Control Applications"
  authors:
